1
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:08,760
YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU,

2
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:09,730
YAMU,

3
00:00:09,813 --> 00:00:16,760
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

5
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:15,377
I don't

6
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:22,460
know.

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,830
Huh?

8
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,030
Kaiba!

9
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:35,200
Call off your dragon, I give, I give!

10
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:36,840
Poor scared Joey.

11
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:41,748
He calls himself a duelist, but he's
just a little puppy dog cringing in fear.

12
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:43,560
I'm not scared of you.

13
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:46,260
Bad dog, don't contradict your master.

14
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,468
You're not my - Quiet, sit.

15
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,190
Huh?

16
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:54,900
Sit at your master's
feet, where you belong.

17
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:06,570
Huh?

18
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:08,050
Ah.

19
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:10,460
A dream.

20
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:16,676
Kaiba, we'll see who he's
the dog chow on this island.

21
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:18,740
Everybody, wake up.

22
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,260
Joey, what's wrong? What is it, Joey?

23
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:23,040
Nah, nothing's wrong.

24
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:28,040
It's just a brand new day at a
tournament, and I'm hot to find us a duel.

25
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,917
Well, you don't have to yell about it.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Hey, guys.

27
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:32,851
What's all the commotion?

28
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,657
Good morning, Taya.

29
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:35,570
Where's Mai?

30
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:36,797
Isn't she with you?

31
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:38,240
She said she had to go.

32
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:40,422
And to give you this note, Yuki.

33
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:41,990
Huh?

34
00:02:42,073 --> 00:02:42,903
Huh?

35
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,520
I owe you eight star chips.

36
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,080
See you around, Mai.

37
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:49,500
Oh, kiss those chips goodbye.

38
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:51,380
I don't know.

39
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,780
Maybe we really can trust Mai.

40
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:58,760
And if not, well, we're still
the Team Supreme, right? Right.

41
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:01,100
Okay, then. Move out.

42
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:03,550
Hmm.

43
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:13,394
I wonder how many duelists
there are left on the island.

44
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:15,717
They shipped a couple
dozen home yesterday.

45
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:18,417
And I bet even more have
been eliminated by now.

46
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:22,437
And some of them were really good
players with powerful cards, too.

47
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,720
We could be next.

48
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:25,340
Not a chance, Yug.

49
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:27,237
Those other guys just wanted the prize.

50
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:29,357
You and Joey have a lot more at stake.

51
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,270
That's true.

52
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:32,357
I've got to rescue Grandpa from Pegasus,

53
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:34,677
and Joey needs the prize
money to help his sister.

54
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:37,920
And the duelists we face
today will be even stronger,

55
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:40,295
because they survived the first round.

56
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:41,840
Even stronger?

57
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:44,368
Careful what you say, Yugi.

58
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:47,157
You've got little Joey here
shaking in his sneakers.

59
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:48,070
What?

60
00:03:48,153 --> 00:03:49,157
You think I'm a scared little puppy dog?

61
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,877
Well, if the collar fits...

62
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,560
All right, break it up.

63
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:55,320
Hey, you just bring on any duelist.

64
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:56,800
Then I'll cream him.

65
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:58,330
Right.

66
00:03:58,413 --> 00:04:00,518
You gotta believe in yourself, Joey.

67
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:01,577
Yeah, that's right.

68
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:03,200
Cause nobody else does.

69
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,080
I want that one.

70
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:12,660
If you like him tall, skinny and stupid
bones, that geek one sure fits the bill.

71
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,780
Oh, yeah, you'll demolish him.

72
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:23,940
So, who are they anyway?

73
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:27,240
Will you just keep your shirt on, Sid?

74
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:30,217
I'm trying to see if I can
get a tighter focus on him.

75
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,157
Hey, me as well.

76
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:34,857
Don't know who the others are, but I
think that little runt is that Yugi kid.

77
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:35,770
Yugi?

78
00:04:35,853 --> 00:04:37,187
He's the one who beat Kaiba.

79
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:38,410
Really?

80
00:04:38,493 --> 00:04:41,780
We better tell the boss
about this, Saigur. Right on.

81
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:49,160
Alright, spit it out.

82
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:50,840
We found two duelists.

83
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,597
One's just a stupid git.

84
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:54,760
But the other one's a good duelist.

85
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,744
That kid's name is Yugi, right?

86
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:59,317
He's the kid who beat Kaiba.

87
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:03,165
Everybody figures him to make it
all the way to Pegasus' castle.

88
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,050
Yugi, huh?

89
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:06,560
Yeah, I heard of him.

90
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,317
He's supposed to be a tough little squirt.

91
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:13,380
That is, if you believe in his
reputation. Huh? Yeah. Yeah!

92
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:15,053
We never seen him duel.

93
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:17,297
How do we know how good Yugi really is?

94
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:18,210
Right.

95
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:20,417
Nobody's going to the castle except us,

96
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:21,817
because we're teamed up with the most

97
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:24,657
brilliant bloomin' duelist
on the whole island.

98
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:25,570
That's right.

99
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:29,817
So if you bums want to win this
tournament, you'll keep your traps shut.

100
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:34,312
You'll keep cool, and you'll let Bandit
Keith do all your thinking for you.

101
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:36,440
No argument from me, boss.

102
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,233
You got all the brains.

103
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:39,520
I'm just a muscle.

104
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:42,997
And we'll hammer any blinkin'
duelist who gets in our way.

105
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:43,910
Any blinkin' duelist.

106
00:05:43,993 --> 00:05:45,018
Hear that, Pegasus?

107
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:46,808
Soon it'll be payback time.

108
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:50,137
Payback for the way you
humiliated me at the

109
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:52,757
Duel Monsters
Intercontinental Championship.

110
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:57,487
It had all come down to you against me,
and I had you right where I wanted you.

111
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:00,610
Ha!

112
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:02,320
Any final words, mullet head?

113
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:04,600
I was sure I was about to win,

114
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:08,597
but you just scribbled some notes and
called over a kid from the audience.

115
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:10,092
Hey, what are you doing?

116
00:06:10,380 --> 00:06:11,909
Asking for help's illegal!

117
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,020
I don't need help.

118
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,757
A child could defeat you, Bandit Keith.

119
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:18,520
and I'm going to prove it.

120
00:06:18,940 --> 00:06:21,646
Just follow these
instructions and you'll win.

121
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,697
I didn't know what to make of it.

122
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:27,917
Were you just trying to psych
me out or did you chicken out?

123
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:32,059
Either way, it was fine by me so
long as I took home the prize money.

124
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:34,300
Okay, punk, beat this.

125
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:37,740
Good car, but the note
says when you play that,

126
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,235
I should play this one in attack mode.

127
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:41,720
No way!

128
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,967
Uh, I think I just took
all your life points.

129
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,390
What?

130
00:06:46,473 --> 00:06:47,797
You little snot-nosed brat.

131
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:50,717
There's no way you could have known
I was going to play that card.

132
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:51,630
Give me that.

133
00:06:51,713 --> 00:06:52,543
Huh?

134
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:54,600
It's all here.

135
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:57,368
The card I play, how
to beat it, everything.

136
00:06:57,460 --> 00:06:58,740
Sam is the winner.

137
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:03,020
You may have defeated
me, Pegasus. Cheated me.

138
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:06,140
But nobody makes a fool out of Bandit Key.

139
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:09,036
Now, you said you found two duelists?

140
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,900
Yeah, Yuki and some dweeb named Joey.

141
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,270
Good.

142
00:07:13,353 --> 00:07:14,864
We'll take the dweeb out first.

143
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:18,439
Did you hear that?

144
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:20,446
I think we're being followed.

145
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:23,977
I think that you're getting
a little paranoid, Joey.

146
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:27,037
You've been acting hyper ever
since you woke up this morning.

147
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,473
Man, what the heck is eating you anyway?

148
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:32,460
I'm telling you, somebody's stalking us.

149
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:34,516
Where are you going?

150
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:35,680
To stalk them!

151
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,980
Boss, where are we headed?

152
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:47,660
To a hidden arena.

153
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,040
In a cave?

154
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:59,082
You ought to feel right
at home down here, Bones.

155
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,597
It's dark and dank and really
creepy just like you are.

156
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:07,220
Your deck, uh, you did load it up
mostly with zombie cards, didn't you?

157
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:08,920
Uh, yeah.

158
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:11,085
Let me see what you got there.

159
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:18,197
Good, but I think you could
use a little more brute force.

160
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:19,817
But where could I find...

161
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:21,180
Don't you worry, kid.

162
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:25,437
I got all the power you
need right here to build

163
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:28,520
the strongest zombie deck
in Duel Monsters history.

164
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:32,154
It's time we moved on to the graveyard.

165
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:34,080
The Graveyard?

166
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:37,620
It's a perfect arena for you, Bones.

167
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:41,253
And with all these new zombie
cards, you just can't lose.

168
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:42,920
Thanks, boss.

169
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:45,780
And you can bet that I won't let you down.

170
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:49,837
You better not or you're gonna
find yourself in a world of hurt.

171
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:52,155
You wouldn't want that now, would you?

172
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:01,157
What are you afraid of?

173
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:03,820
Some musty old skull. Yeah.

174
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,021
Give me a break.

175
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:07,532
Your face is scarier than this old thing.

176
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:13,440
Uh, boss, wait for me.

177
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,720
Maybe Paya was right.

178
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:19,195
I guess all I heard was the waterfall.

179
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:21,440
Can I help you?

180
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:25,780
Wake up, dweeb.

181
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:28,930
You!

182
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,100
What? Where am I?

183
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:35,600
The boss wants you off!

184
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,960
What is this place?

185
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,320
A tombstone?

186
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:55,500
Welcome, duelists, to
the arena of lost souls.

187
00:09:57,620 --> 00:10:01,640
Abandon hope, for no duelist
gets out of here alive.

188
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,260
Help, my ghost!

189
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:14,657
Joey's been gone an awfully long time.

190
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:16,437
You don't suppose he got lost?

191
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:19,557
No way, but he could have
been challenged to a duel.

192
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:20,780
I bet that's it.

193
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:24,397
I must have gotten his case a
little too hard about being scared,

194
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:27,417
So now he's gone off to
fight a duel all by himself.

195
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:30,380
Okay, let's split up and
try to find him. Right.

196
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:32,801
Yugi and Teya, you head that way.

197
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:34,397
Bakura and I will go this way.

198
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:35,310
Okay.

199
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:41,640
Prepare for your final duel.

200
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:45,060
This arena will be your graveyard.

201
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:46,940
Ooh, spooky.

202
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:48,820
Spot on, mate.

203
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:51,082
He's got the dweeb scared stiff.

204
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:52,697
I don't believe it.

205
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:55,200
Looks like the guy fainted on his feet.

206
00:10:56,260 --> 00:10:58,300
Yeah, so do something, Sigour.

207
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,400
Get busy and wake him up.

208
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:01,900
You heard him, dweeb.

209
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:02,980
Rise and shine.

210
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:07,900
The ghosts of the dead
are all around you, Joey.

211
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:10,980
There's no way to escape from your fear.

212
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:12,530
Huh?

213
00:11:12,613 --> 00:11:13,640
Who says I'm scared?

214
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:16,980
You can't hide the truth
from the spirits, Joey.

215
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:20,080
Wow, they see you frozen in fear.

216
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:22,380
Okay, I was afraid.

217
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:26,074
But not because of the graveyard
or your ooga-booga rap.

218
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:29,200
It's your creepy face
that gave me the willies!

219
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:32,517
You have to admit he's got a point, Bones.

220
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:36,280
Yeah, you even spooked me out,
Bones, and I'm on your side.

221
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:40,820
Well, if you're on my side,
then stop laughing at me!

222
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:43,897
So are we going to duel or
just stand around talking?

223
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:45,686
Lay down your star chips now!

224
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:50,520
Hey, I never even agreed
to this duel. Tough luck.

225
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:52,820
You haven't got any choice, dweeb.

226
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:57,900
There has to be some way out of this!

227
00:11:58,540 --> 00:11:59,370
Huh?

228
00:11:59,453 --> 00:12:00,440
You want a way out?

229
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:04,957
We'll hand over all your star chips and
crawl out like a scared little puppy dog!

230
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:06,540
Bad doggy!

231
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:09,880
Puppy dog?

232
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:14,420
Sit at your master's
feet, where you belong!

233
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:21,906
If I run from this, I really will
be a scared little puppy dog.

234
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:24,140
So I'll just have to beat you

235
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:26,300
Four star chips

236
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:29,737
Nice going boss.

237
00:12:29,820 --> 00:12:31,080
He fell for it

238
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:33,760
Let's do

239
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:40,117
Put him away quick bones send him
straight to the grave with a zombie card.

240
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:42,120
Yeah a zombie card

241
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:47,000
Yikes now I get what he's up
to you don't stand a chance

242
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:49,660
This arena's one big graveyard field.

243
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:53,340
And all my zombie cards get
a field power bonus here.

244
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:55,800
Joey? Joey?

245
00:12:57,540 --> 00:12:59,422
There's no sign of him anywhere.

246
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:01,525
Hey, let's look over that way.

247
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:04,270
Joey?

248
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:05,730
Joey!

249
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:08,420
He's not here.

250
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:09,517
Where could he be?

251
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:13,188
If he were fighting a duel, I'm
sure that we'd see the arena.

252
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:14,800
Joey's just vanished.

253
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:16,300
I'm worried, Taya.

254
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:26,597
here goes my zombie card not so fast

255
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:30,837
hold that card for now play the one on the

256
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:33,997
far left instead play the one on the left

257
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:38,757
boss but that card is zanky zanky's not a

258
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:43,617
zombie card at all you needed some raw
muscle so i slipped it into your deck bones

259
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:48,641
but if it's not a zombie card it won't get
the field power bonus from the graveyard.

260
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,337
Don't argue with me, Squirt.

